<section class="section surface" id="my-story"><div class="container personal-story-grid">
 <div><span class="eyebrow">My beginnings</span><h2>Born in Nyeri.<br>Shaped by Endarasha.</h2><p class="personal-story-lead">I was born in the heart of Nyeri Town. My childhood took me to the boundary of Gakanga and Charity sub-locations in the picturesque Endarasha Location, at the foot of the Nyandarua Mountains, looking towards magnificent Mount Kenya.</p></div>
 <div class="personal-story-copy"><p>I began primary school at Gakanga Primary School, on the edges of Aberdares National Park. Land, water, farming, roads and markets were part of the world around me long before they became subjects I would think and write about.</p><p>Those early surroundings still shape my interest in livelihoods, opportunity and the environment. I now look at them alongside the questions that enterprise brings: who can participate, what gets in the way, and how can a useful idea become something that lasts?</p><a class="text-link" href="<?=url('/my-thoughts')?>">Explore the questions in My Thoughts →</a></div>
</div></section>
<section class="section" id="education"><div class="container personal-story-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Education & opportunity</span><h2>People opened doors.<br>I kept learning.</h2><p>My education was not a straight line. It crossed different places, institutions and circumstances, The Salesians of Don Bosco paid for my full high school education, giving me the opportunity to continue learning through each of those stages.</p></div><ol class="personal-timeline">
 <li><span>01 · Nyeri</span><h3>Gakanga Primary School</h3><p>My first classroom, near Aberdares National Park and the landscape of Endarasha.</p></li>
 <li><span>02 · Nairobi</span><h3>Morrisson Primary School & Bosco Boys</h3><p>After moving to Nairobi, I briefly attended Morrisson Primary School in Bahati. I was later fortunate to be welcomed at Bosco Boys Nairobi by the Salesians of Don Bosco, who paid for my entire high school education.</p></li>
 <li><span>03 · Baringo & Meru</span><h3>Christ the King & St. Pius X</h3><p>I spent one year at Christ the King High School in Mogotio, Baringo County, and another at St. Pius X Seminary in Nkubu, Meru County.</p></li>
 <li><span>04 · Nairobi</span><h3>Muhuri Muchiri High School</h3><p>I completed my high school education at Muhuri Muchiri High School in Ruai, Nairobi County.</p></li>
 <li><span>05 · University education</span><h3>The Riara University</h3><p>I am an alumnus of The Riara University. This is part of my formal education.</p></li><li><span>06 · Real-life experience</span><h3>“Mjengo University”</h3><p>This is my name for learning through real life: work, building businesses, setbacks, responsibility and the experience that comes from doing. It is separate from my university education.</p></li>
 </ol></div></section>
<section class="section surface" id="business-lessons"><div class="container personal-story-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">Lessons earned in business</span><h2>I have failed.<br>I still believe in enterprise.</h2><p class="personal-story-lead">Starting a business without capital sitting in a bank is not for the faint-hearted. I know that through experience.</p></div><div class="personal-story-copy"><p>There have been late salaries, delayed payments to suppliers, customers who did not pay, and difficult experiences with banks and the terms of finance. These are not abstract business-school cases for me. They affect people, relationships and trust.</p><p>I have learned from those failures and pressures. They have made me more attentive to cash flow, commitments, the cost of capital and the gap between an attractive idea and a business that can support itself.</p><p>My passion for social entrepreneurship remains. I want to use the experience I now have to build more carefully, test assumptions earlier and create enterprises that are commercially viable, socially useful and environmentally responsible.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section personal-build-section" id="building-together"><div class="container"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Building together</span><h2>Walk the journey with me.</h2></div><p>I want this readership to be part of the learning: following the questions, the small tests, the difficult decisions and the progress towards Goal 2030.</p></div><div class="experience-grid">
 <article class="experience-card"><span class="eyebrow">Listen first</span><h3>Understand the problem</h3><p>Start with people and their circumstances. Ask what matters before deciding what to build.</p><a class="text-link" href="<?=url('/resources/problem-interview-worksheet')?>">Use the interview worksheet →</a></article>
 <article class="experience-card"><span class="eyebrow">Build lean</span><h3>Test before committing more</h3><p>Make the next step small enough to learn from. Examine demand, cost and what customers are willing to do.</p><a class="text-link" href="<?=url('/startup-journeys')?>">Follow Startup Journeys →</a></article>
 <article class="experience-card"><span class="eyebrow">Learn openly</span><h3>Record what changed</h3><p>Share the evidence, successes, setbacks and next decisions as reviewed chapters and reports are published.</p><a class="text-link" href="<?=url('/newsletter')?>">Receive new writing →</a></article>
